  "description": "MIT AST AudioSet Classifier serves MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593 through a Forge-owned FastAPI wrapper for short WAV, FLAC, MP3, or OGG clips. The upstream model is an Audio Spectrogram Transformer fine-tuned on AudioSet and exposes 527 AudioSet labels, including Cough at index 47, Throat clearing, Sneeze, Wheeze, and Breathing. Hugging Face metadata checked on 2026-07-06 reports private=false, gated=false, disabled=false, license bsd-3-clause, library_name=transformers, pipeline_tag=audio-classification, tags including audio-spectrogram-transformer and arxiv:2104.01778, revision f826b80d28226b62986cc218e5cec390b1096902, ASTForAudioClassification architecture, ASTFeatureExtractor preprocessor at 16 kHz, and model.safetensors LFS SHA256 ae0c1e2ad4e1381d851fa9bf298ba13ebc9c5a914cdee2dbe427a6583869924d. The wrapper verifies the pinned safetensors checkpoint before loading, stores Hugging Face, Transformers, Torch, XDG, and HOME caches under shared /mnt/data/forge-weights, exposes /audio_classification, /v1/audio_classification, /run, and /v1/health/ready, accepts audio_data data URI/base64 inputs plus guarded public HTTPS audio_url inputs, returns sorted sigmoid label scores with duration/sample-rate metadata and model_time_ms, and explicitly rejects frame scores because AST does not expose calibrated frame-level scores. The model was promoted after HCLS safety signoff; live upsert and real GPU matrix probes passed on 2026-07-06.",
